{
    "background_story": "Kaliyah was a talented painter known for her captivating portraits. However, it was her subtle use of subfigures that set her apart from her contemporaries. In her most famous piece, 'The Gathering,' a crowd of people seemed to be the main focus, but upon closer inspection, a small, almost imperceptible figure in the corner caught the viewer's eye. This tiny figure, a young girl lost in thought, was the true subject of the painting. Kaliyah's use of subfigures added layers of depth and meaning to her work, inviting viewers to explore beyond the surface level. As her reputation grew, so did her fascination with the power of subtle storytelling, leading her to create an entire series of works that celebrated the beauty of the overlooked and the unseen.",
